{"id":1463,"root":"لحي","bw":"lHy","tr":"l-ḥ-y","found":true,"html":"<div class=\"lane-entry\">See Supplement </div><div class=\"lane-entry\"> <span class=\"lane-form\">  <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">لُحِىَ</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">*</span> </span>: see a verse cited voce <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">خَطَبَ</span>. ― -b2- <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">لَحَاهُ اللّٰهُ</span>: see <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">شَرَاهُ</span>. </div><div class=\"lane-entry\"> <span class=\"lane-form\">  <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">تَلَحَّى</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">*</span> </span>, (S, Mgh,) and <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">تلحّى بِعِمَامَتِهِ</span>, (TA, art. <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">عجر</span>,) <em>He wound a part of his turban under his lower jaw:</em> (S, Mgh:) as also <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">تَحَنَّكَ</span>, q. v. </div><div class=\"lane-entry\"> <span class=\"lane-form\">  <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">اِلْتَحَيتُ اللَّحْمَ عَنِ العَظْمِ</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">*</span> </span> [<em>I peeled off the flesh from the bone</em>]. (O, K, in art. <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">سلق</span>.) </div><div class=\"lane-entry\"> <span class=\"lane-form\"> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">لَحْىٌ</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">*</span> </span> [not <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">لَحًى</span>] The <em>jaw-bone;</em> (Mgh, Msb;) either <em>upper or lower:</em> (Msb:) and, in a man, (Msb,) the <em>part on which the beard grows.</em> (S, Msb, K.) ― -b2- And sometimes <em>Either lateral portion of the lower jaw:</em> see <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">ذَقَنٌ</span>, and <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">الفَنِيكُ</span>. </div><div class=\"lane-entry\"> <span class=\"lane-form\"> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">لِحْيَةُ التَّيسِ</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">*</span> </span>: see <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">ثِيلٌ</span>. ― -b2- <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">لِحْيَةٌ</span> is sometimes, by a synecdoche, put for the whole <em>person:</em> see a verse cited voce <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">خُنْثٌ</span>. </div><div class=\"lane-entry\"> <span class=\"lane-form\"> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">مَسْحُ اللُِّحَى</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">*</span> </span>: see <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">عَقَّ بِالسَّهْمِ</span>. </div><div class=\"lane-entry\"> <span class=\"lane-form\"> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">لِحَاءٌ</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">*</span> </span> <em>Bark;</em> and in particular the <em>bark</em> of a plant, or of a tree, <em>of which ropes &amp;c. are made.</em> ― -b2- The <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">لِحَاء</span> of the date is [its <em>Pulp, pulpy pericarp,</em> or <em>flesh;</em> i. e.] the <em>part that clothes the</em> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">نَوَاة</span> [or <em>stone</em>]. (TA.) ― -b3- <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">لِحَاءُ العِنَبِ</span> [<em>The skin of grapes</em>]. (TA in art. <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">شحم</span>.) </div><div class=\"lane-entry\"> <span class=\"lane-form\"> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">لَوَاحِى الشَّيبِ</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">*</span> </span>, for <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">لَوَايءِحُ الشيب</span>, q. v. </div>","pages":null,"shownPages":null,"chars":2177,"entries":9,"shownEntries":9,"truncated":false,"match":"direct","key":"lHy"}